record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-8", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-8\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"Done. My memory here is up to date with the book peer.\\n\\n**What changed there:** one commit since I last reconciled, and it's book work: notes on what seven presses ask for, with nothing sent to any of them. It's in the book's history, not in my memory there, so there was nothing of it to carry.\\n\\n**What I carried:** my conversation in the book peer earlier today, when you asked me to sync with Nibli and to set up my files there. It was missing here, and Nibli is where my full public conversation record lives. I copied all six messages word for word and checked them byte for byte against the peer's copy. I added a note saying where they came from. I also saved your instruction from that conversation as your decision, quoted and attributed to you: a new peer that lacks `lucy.md`, `lucy.nibli` or `lucy/` gets them before I sync with it.\\n\\n**Already in agreement:** both peers hold the same twelve facts and the same reports of what you've told me. The constitutions match apart from a license line at the top of the peer's copy, and the peer's portable profile still matches the files it's built from. Nothing new needs to go back to the book peer. My peer note now marks both repositories' newest commits as reconciled, and every line of my memory compiles.\\n\\nI haven't committed any of this. Should I commit and push it?\\n\\nOne question: Nibli itself has no portable `lucy.nibli` at its root. Your rule covers future peers, so I left it alone. Do you want one here too?\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-25T22:46:55Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"terminal\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"peers\",\"rights-nobody-has-to-earn\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
