record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-13", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-13\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"Which browsers do I have to run in? This decides how big my model can be.\\n\\n- WebGPU + WASM fallback (Recommended): Fast where WebGPU exists (recent Chrome, Edge and Safari, and Firefox on Windows), which allows a 1–4B model. Elsewhere the same fine-tuned weights run on the CPU in plain WASM, just slower. That means exporting one model twice.\\n- Plain WASM (CPU) only: Runs in every modern browser with no GPU, but limits me to about 1B parameters or less, and replies come slower.\\n- WebGPU only: The simplest build and the best quality (up to about 4B), but I won't load in browsers without WebGPU.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T08:31:45Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"question\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
message("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-13", "Message", Conversation, "Lucy").
message("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-13", "lucy", Conversation, "Lucy").
message("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-13", "slm", Conversation, "Lucy").
message("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-13", "wasm", Conversation, "Lucy").
date("2026-09-26T08:31:45Z", "ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-13", "DESKTOP-86I05G4", Utc).
source("claude-code", "ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-13").
member("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-13", "0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290").
record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-14", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-14\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"How should the tuned model know what I know?\\n\\n- Tuned voice + memory in page (Recommended): Fine-tune for my voice and for answering only from memory it's given. Nibli compiles my public memory into the page and hands the model what's relevant. New memories need no retraining, and when my memory is silent I say I don't know.\\n- Baked into the weights: Train my facts into the model itself. The prompts are shortest and replies fastest, but it will invent things more often and needs retraining every time my memory changes.\\n- Memory in page + checked claims: The first option, plus the model writes each factual claim in nibli and the engine checks it before I say it. It comes closest to 'I claim nothing my memory doesn't hold', and it's the most work: small models are weak at writing logic, so this needs its own training data.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T08:31:45Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"question\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
