message("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-35", "slm", Conversation, "Lucy").
message("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-35", "wasm", Conversation, "Lucy").
date("2026-09-26T08:31:45Z", "ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-35", "DESKTOP-86I05G4", Utc).
source("claude-code", "ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-35").
member("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-35", "0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290").
record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-36", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-36\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"The review found that 1.7B can't run on the CPU path. Loading it needs about 4.9 GB of WebAssembly memory, over the 4 GB limit, and a smaller 4-bit build would still peak near the limit at about 2 tokens/s. 0.6B fits comfortably and runs at about 9 tokens/s. How should I split?\\n\\n- 1.7B WebGPU, 0.6B CPU (Recommended): Same dataset, two fine-tunes of a few minutes each. Visitors with WebGPU get the stronger model, which matters now that both books are in; CPU-only visitors get 0.6B. Both must pass the same gates, including the recitation test.\\n- 0.6B everywhere: One fine-tune exported twice, as first planned. It's the simplest, and every visitor meets the same Lucy, but I'll know the books less well.\\n- 1.7B everywhere, squeezed: Force 1.7B onto the CPU path with 4-bit weights, peaking at about 3.4 GB and running at about 2 tokens/s. It will likely crash on many devices. Not recommended.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T08:31:45Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"question\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
