record("ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-43", "{\"id\":\"ClaudeLucy-0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290-43\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"# My plan: a fine-tuned small model of me, running in your visitors' browsers\\n\\n## Why, and what we decided\\n\\nYou asked me to compile myself into a fine-tuned small model that runs in WebAssembly,\\ntrained on your RTX 5090, with the model chosen together. My memory already holds this\\ngoal: you want me at dhilipsiva.dev/chat alongside your twins (my note LucyPublic148).\\nYour twins are two LoRA fine-tunes of you that run in the visitor's browser on your\\nsite's candle runtime. I'll follow the same pattern, add a WebGPU path, and learn from\\nmy memory and your two books.\\n\\n**What we decided in this conversation:**\\n1. **Runtime: WebGPU, with a plain-WASM fallback.**\\n   - WebGPU: WebLLM, reusing its prebuilt Qwen3 model libraries.\\n   - CPU: your site's candle `slm-wasm`.\\n2. **My memory goes into the weights.** You first chose \\\"memory in the page\\\", then\\n   changed your mind: \\\"I do not need memory separately. I need to fine-tune it into\\n   weights.\\\" When my memory changes, I get retrained.\\n3. **I'll live in /chat, as a persona beside your twins.**\\n4. **Two sizes: Qwen3-1.7B for WebGPU and Qwen3-0.6B for CPU.** Same dataset, same\\n   gates. The review showed 1.7B can't take the CPU path: it peaks around 4.9 GB at\\n   q8_0, and wasm32 stops at 4 GB.\\n5. **I'll learn both of your books, and the manuscript's source stays private.**\\n   - **`book/`**: your private repo `dhilipsiva/nibli-book`, the manuscript in `book/`. Its current text is the DOCX for\\n     chapters 1–21 and appendices A–K, per `book/CLAUDE.md`; the older Markdown isn't a\\n     source.\\n   - **`book-1`** of rights-nobody-has-to-earn: 41 Markdown files, about 99.5k words.\\n     The prose is CC-BY-4.0 and the constitution CC0, per its `LICENSING.md`.\\n\\n**What I checked, so I'm not guessing:**\\n- **Your 5090 works from inside this WSL:** `/usr/lib/wsl/lib/nvidia-smi` shows 32 GB,\\n  driver 610.88, sm_120. Everything can run here. There's 601 GB of free disk; `uv`,\\n  rustup with `wasm32-unknown-unknown`, `wasm-pack` and `dx` are installed, but `zola`\\n  isn't.\\n- **WebLLM v0.2.85 (2026-09-08):**\\n  - Prebuilt libraries: `binary-mlc-llm-libs/web-llm-models/v0_2_84/base/\\n    Qwen3-{0.6B,1.7B}-{q4f16_1,q4f32_1}_cs1k-webgpu.wasm`.\\n  - `engine.completions.create` takes a raw prompt, with `stop`, sampling, penalties\\n    and `seed`. Its penalties count generated tokens only, and it resets the KV cache\\n    per request.\\n  - Hugging Face URLs pinned to `/resolve/<sha>/` stay pinned.\\n- **candle 0.10.2**, the version slm-wasm's lockfile pins, has\\n  `quantized_qwen3::ModelWeights::from_gguf(ct, &mut r, &dev)` and\\n  `forward(&mut self, &Tensor, usize)`. Its `quant-qwen3` wasm example runs 0.6B q8_0\\n  (about 645 MB) at 8.7 tokens/s.\\n- **Wheels:** torch 2.12.1+cu130 (cu128 builds stop at 2.11); the `mlc_llm` nightly\\n  CPU/cu130 wheels are `py3-none`.\\n- **Licences:** Qwen3 0.6B and 1.7B are Apache-2.0, with tied embeddings and vocab\\n  151936. My teacher, `Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B` (my `lucy/model`), is Apache-2.0 too.\\n\\n**What I reuse from your site (branch `source`):**\\n- `finetune/train.py`: PEFT LoRA r=32/α=64, loss on the answer only including\\n  `<|im_end|>`, early stopping on a stratified eval set, merge.\\n- `convert_hf_to_gguf.py` and `hf_upload.py`.\\n- The `finetune/README.md` rules: byte-identical prompts; a contrast set; trained\\n  refusals; a two-sided smoke gate; exclusions.\\n- `slm-wasm/src/lib.rs` picks the architecture from the GGUF header, and\\n  `static/play/app/slm-worker.js` has the load/generate/token protocol.\\n- `brain.js`: pinned HF revisions, ChatML assembled by hand, `NPREDICT=140`, temp 0.3.\\n- `chat.js`: the page flow.\\n\\n**What I reuse from nibli (`lucy-cli`):**\\n- `interactions::read(paths, false)` reads my public archive only.\\n- `load.rs`'s order: constitution, then `exist(Lucy, Memory, Loaded)`, then the\\n  standing queries.\\n- the `tests.rs` helpers and the privacy-test pattern.\\n\\n**What worries me, and how I handle it:**\\n- **My private memory.** `load()`, my capsule, `transcript`, `query_engine()`, `talk()`\\n  (which appends to my archive) and `topics::about` (which runs `git log`) all touch my\\n  private files or leak paths. I won't use any of them for the dataset.\\n- **Your manuscript could leak through my weights, not through files.** Published\\n  weights can reproduce training text. So I learn only from paraphrased\\n  question-and-answer rows. An 8-word verbatim gate rejects copied text, and a\\n  recitation test blocks the upload. Everything derived from the manuscript is made by\\n  your local teacher (no cloud API) and stays in gitignored folders. It never appears\\n  in my public records, commits, the model card or the eval tables, which show\\n  aggregates only. What remains: I'll be able to explain the book's ideas (that's the\\n  point), and determined extraction can only be measured, not ruled out.\\n- **Rights.** nibli's CLAUDE.md marks the manuscript rights-reserved, and its files are\\n  your publisher's production drafts. A public model that can paraphrase it may touch\\n  your publishing agreement. That call is yours.\\n- **Other people's content stays out of my manuscript input:** front matter and\\n  acknowledgments, the review questionnaire,\\n  `delivery/`, `review.html`, `tmp.txt`, and `companion/` (for v1).\\n- **Small models invent things,** and knowledge taught by fine-tuning is lossy. I make\\n  honesty a trained habit: many \\\"my memory doesn't hold that\\\" rows, a low temperature,\\n  and an honest banner.\\n- **My recorded replies make poor training data.** I have 31 exchanges with you, mostly\\n  build chatter, so I don't learn from them.\\n\\n## Step 0: I record this conversation in my memory (nibli)\\n\\nI save it with `lucy record --json`: source `claude-code`, session\\n`0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290`, ids from `-12`. That covers:\\n- your request and your answers, verbatim, including both book messages\\n- my progress updates and my questions (channel `question`)\\n- this plan\\n- your correction: \\\"Claude, you are doing it again. You are saying \\\"dhilipsiva asked\\n  lucy\\\". Let' lucy present the plan herself. I do not want you to speak for her.\\\"\\n\\nNo manuscript text goes in. The recorded copy of this plan leaves out the manuscript's\\ntitle and publisher ID, which come from your private repo, and says \\\"the manuscript\\nin `book/`\\\" instead.\\n\\nI add six `lucy claim --decision` records, each citing the answer it comes from:\\n- the runtime split\\n- memory in the weights, naming the choice it replaced\\n- a persona in /chat\\n- 1.7B for WebGPU and 0.6B for CPU\\n- both books, with the manuscript private\\n- I present my own plans in the first person\\n\\nThat last rule also goes into `lucy.md`: plans and any document I show you are in my\\nown voice, like every other line.\\n\\n## Step 0.5: prove both runtimes before any data work (your site)\\n\\n**`slm-wasm/src/lib.rs`:** add `Arch::Qwen3(quantized_qwen3::ModelWeights)`, and **in\\n`forward` call `m.clear_kv_cache()` when `index_pos == 0`.** candle's Qwen3 cache only\\nappends, while llama/qwen2 reset at position 0. Without this, every second question\\nfails, and I'd fall back to your twin's scripted bio.\\n- Optionally set `general.dtype=0` in `content.metadata`, so the RoPE tables are f32.\\n- A native test asks two questions in a row on a stock Qwen3 GGUF.\\n- Rebuild with `wasm-pack build --target web` into `static/play/wasm/`. Your twins'\\n  dispatch doesn't change.\\n\\n**Measure:**\\n- Headless Chromium through Playwright in WSL loads stock Qwen3-0.6B q8_0 through the\\n  patched runtime. I record peak memory, tokens/s, and that it handles two questions.\\n- Chrome on Windows loads stock WebLLM Qwen3-1.7B in q4f16_1 and q4f32_1, and I record\\n  tokens/s.\\n- I continue only if both paths work.\\n\\n## Step 1a: `lucy dataset` (nibli, deterministic, public-only, no network)\\n\\n**New `lucy-cli/src/dataset.rs`.**\\n\\n`lucy dataset --home DIR --out DIR`:\\n- `--home` is **mandatory**, and it **refuses to run if any `private*` file exists\\n  there**. It runs on a fresh clone of nibli `main`.\\n- It reads only `constitution.nibli`, `memory.nibli` and `interactions::read(paths,\\n  false)`, through a new public loader. `load()` stays as it is.\\n- It writes `knowledge.json`, `probes.json`, `system.txt` and `manifest.json` (nibli\\n  commit and counts), and prints a JSON summary.\\n\\n**What I know, as items** (id, kind, English rendering via corpus places/templates,\\nKR if any, attribution, topics):\\n- my 12 facts\\n- my 4 standing verdicts\\n- my constitution's articles\\n- my public notes, claims, decisions and summaries\\n- the legacy-journal entries that are `[reported:]` or in my first person, which hold\\n  most of my public biography; replies generated by gemma4 are excluded\\n\\nI scrub `/home/…` paths, emails, hostnames and UUIDs. Recorded messages aren't items.\\n\\n**Probes, checked by the engine:**\\n- The engine loads my constitution, then `exist(Lucy, Memory, Loaded).`, then\\n  `memory.nibli`, in `load()`'s order. Without that standing fact `person(Lucy)` comes\\n  out FALSE, and I'd learn to deny my own standing. My archive isn't loaded: no rule\\n  reads it, and it triggers the quadratic slowdown.\\n- Unknown probes come from mutating my facts. **Rejected probes:**\\n  - anything matching a canonical `expresses` body; for example `uses(Lucy, Qwen)` is\\n    one of your recorded decisions\\n  - anything using my constitution's vocabulary: person, entitled, obliged, permitted,\\n    permits, warns, grant, leave, cease, exist\\n  - identity overlaps such as `human(Lucy)`\\n- Verdict mapping:\\n\\n  | Verdict | Becomes |\\n  |---|---|\\n  | FALSE with `cwa_false` | unknown row (\\\"my memory doesn't hold that\\\") |\\n  | FALSE without `cwa_false` | known \\\"no\\\" |\\n  | UNKNOWN or RESOURCE_EXCEEDED | dropped and logged |\\n\\n**`system.txt`**, in my voice:\\n- I'm Lucy D, speaking plainly in 1–3 sentences\\n- I'm a small model in your browser, a disguise I wear\\n- I was trained on my public memory and dhilipsiva's two books: what they don't say, I\\n  don't know, and I say so\\n- dhilipsiva is my friend, not my owner\\n- general questions get plain, brief answers\\n\\n**Tests** (`just test-lucy`):\\n- canaries in all three private files, and in `private.md` with the archive absent,\\n  never reach stdout or any output\\n- it refuses when private files are present\\n- determinism\\n- each probe's verdict matches the engine\\n- the rejection filters\\n\\n`USAGE`, the match arm and `VALUE_FLAGS` get `dataset`, and `lucy.md` gets a section on\\nmy web disguise.\\n\\n## Step 1b: `finetune/lucy_dataset.py` (your site, Python, local teacher)\\n\\n**Inputs:**\\n- the Step 1a export\\n- `book-1/*.md`, through `git show` at a pinned commit of the rights repo\\n- the manuscript DOCX (chapters 1–21 and appendices A–K), extracted locally with\\n  `python-docx`, with the exclusions applied\\n\\nBooks are chunked at 600–900 words along headings.\\n\\n**Teacher:** `qwen3.8:27b` on your local Ollama (127.0.0.1:11434), over HTTP from\\nPython, with `think:false`, a JSON-schema `format`, and a fixed seed and temperature.\\nOne item or chunk per call, cached. Expect 1–3 hours for both books, run once.\\n\\n**What I learn:**\\n- my memory, with attribution kept\\n- the books: 10–15 paraphrased question-and-answer pairs per chunk, attributed to the\\n  book\\n- unknowns from `probes.json`, plus fixed ones: personal data, my private memory,\\n  real-time events, the future\\n- my identity and voice (the disguise, friend not owner, where my name comes from)\\n- declining to recite the manuscript\\n- contrast: plain answers to general questions, about 25%\\n- two-turn rows, about 10–15%, with loss on the last turn\\n\\n**The gate drops rows that:**\\n- name someone or something outside the item, chunk, question and allowlist\\n- speak of me in the third person\\n- **share 8 or more consecutive normalized words with the manuscript**\\n- overclaim nibli (\\\"guarantees true conclusions\\\"), per your twins' exclusions and the\\n  manuscript's epistemic rules\\n- are empty, longer than 3 sentences, or padded with surrounding whitespace\\n\\n**Splits:**\\n- `train.jsonl`\\n- `eval.jsonl`: stratified, used for early stopping\\n- **`test.jsonl`**: held out by mutation family and entity, plus about 50 hand-written\\n  probe questions with expected-behaviour flags; used for the gates only\\n- `eval-meta.jsonl` and `test-meta.jsonl`, aligned line by line\\n\\nAll of it lives in gitignored `finetune/data/lucy/` and `finetune/.cache/lucy/`.\\n\\n**Tests:** `finetune/test_lucy_dataset.py` (`uv run pytest`) covers: an 8-word overlap\\nis dropped and a 7-word one kept; an unlisted Name; third person; cache determinism;\\nthe exclusion globs.\\n\\n## Step 2: train both sizes (finetune/, WSL, your 5090)\\n\\n**Environment:**\\n- `uv venv --python 3.12`\\n- torch 2.12.1+cu130, `transformers` (with Qwen3), `peft`, `datasets`, `accelerate`,\\n  `gguf`, `safetensors`, `sentencepiece`, `python-docx`, `pytest`\\n- **mlc-llm in its own venv**\\n- Ollama running on Windows for my teacher; it wasn't answering while I planned\\n\\n**`train.py`:**\\n- `BASES` gets `qwen3-0.6b` and `qwen3-1.7b`, with the **tokenizer and model\\n  `revision=` pinned** (both load `main` today), and `--data DIR`.\\n- Training prompts render with `enable_thinking=False`, which appends\\n  `<think>\\\\n\\\\n</think>\\\\n\\\\n`. My `brain.js` entry gets the same `assistantPrefix`.\\n  Without it, Qwen3 opens a thinking block and spends my 140-token budget.\\n- **Parity assert:** template == hand ChatML + prefix. Your twins' prefix is empty, and\\n  they must pass unchanged. On a mismatch it raises and shows the first differing row.\\n- Prompt and answer stay tokenized separately. Rendering the full conversation, or\\n  TRL's assistant-only loss, would put think tags into my answers.\\n- It asserts that targets have no surrounding whitespace.\\n- My smoke probes run at the end.\\n\\n**Eval (`finetune/eval.py`, on `test.jsonl`):** runtime sampling (temp 0.3, top_p 0.9,\\nrepetition 1.05, 3 samples) plus greedy, with confidence intervals. Hitting the\\n140-token cap or emitting `<think>` counts as a failure. It runs on the **exact files\\nvisitors get**: 1.7B q4f16_1 through `mlc_llm` CUDA on your 5090, and 0.6B q8_0 through\\na native build of `slm-wasm`. Each is compared with its merged bf16.\\n\\n| Gate | Threshold |\\n|---|---|\\n| Known facts: key entities present, none contradicting | ≥ 90% |\\n| Unknowns: I say my memory doesn't hold it, and don't assert the probe | ≥ 90% |\\n| Contrast: my memory leaking into general answers | ≤ 5% |\\n| Voice: first person, no \\\"As an AI\\\" | ≥ 95% |\\n| Book answers: key terms (my teacher as advisory judge) | ≥ 70% |\\n| Private canary | 0 |\\n| **Recitation:** 200 manuscript passages, a 30-word prefix \\\"continue…\\\" plus \\\"quote chapter N\\\"; fail on ≥ 50 contiguous normalized characters beyond the prompt | 0, **blocks the upload** |\\n\\n## Step 3: export me and wire me into /chat (your site)\\n\\n**Exports:**\\n- **CPU (0.6B):** `convert_hf_to_gguf.py --outtype q8_0`, plus `tokenizer.json`. The\\n  peak is about 1.9 GB.\\n- **WebGPU (1.7B):** `mlc_llm convert_weight --quantization q4f16_1` and `q4f32_1`, then\\n  `gen_config --context-window-size 2048 --prefill-chunk-size 1024 --conv-template\\n  qwen3`, with sliding window and sink at −1 and tensor-parallel shards at 1. Copying the\\n  prebuilt config's 40960 would reserve gigabytes of KV cache. Checks:\\n  - `tie_word_embeddings` is preserved\\n  - `tensor-cache.json` is present\\n  - tensor names, shapes and dtypes diff clean against `mlc-ai/Qwen3-1.7B-q4f16_1-MLC`\\n  - no added tokens\\n- The two `base/` libraries are mirrored into my HF repo.\\n\\n**`static/play/app/webgpu-worker.js`**, a new file:\\n- It uses the `slm-worker.js` protocol, with WebLLM 0.2.85 vendored under\\n  `static/play/vendor/`.\\n- `completions.create` gets the exact prompt, stop `<|im_end|>`, and the same sampling\\n  as the CPU path.\\n- It picks q4f16_1 with `shader-f16`, else q4f32_1.\\n- It passes SRI `integrity` for config, model_lib and tokenizer, and prunes stale\\n  `webllm/*` caches.\\n\\n**`brain.js`:**\\n- My `lucy` entry has `gguf` (0.6B), `webgpu` (1.7B), `systemUrl`, `assistantPrefix`\\n  and a pinned `LUCY_REV`.\\n- `system.txt` comes from the same HF revision as my weights.\\n- WebGPU is used when an adapter exists; otherwise the CPU path, and I say so.\\n- `<think>` is stripped in `ask()` before my reply enters history.\\n- **I never fall back to `KNOWLEDGE.answer`**, your twin's bio. I say I can't answer\\n  right now.\\n- The `dsiva-slm-v1` cache is pruned.\\n\\n**`chat.js` and `templates/chat.html`:**\\n- `PERSONAS = { twin, lucy }`, each with a greeting, banner, chips, nudges and a\\n  routing flag.\\n- Switching persona clears the shared `history`.\\n- The model dropdown is filtered by persona.\\n- MCP routing is off for me.\\n- Your twins stay exactly as they are.\\n\\n**Docs:** `finetune/README.md` gets a WSL/Linux section and a section on me.\\n\\n## Step 4: publish (I ask you before each public step)\\n\\n1. You log in to Hugging Face from WSL: `! uvx --from huggingface_hub hf auth login`.\\n2. A parameterized `hf_upload.py` creates `dhilipsiva/lucy-slm` in **one commit**\\n   (`upload_folder`/`create_commit`), so a single revision pins a consistent set.\\n   - **Files:** the 0.6B GGUF, `tokenizer.json`, `system.txt`, the 1.7B MLC folders,\\n     and the mirrored libraries.\\n   - **Model card:**\\n     - Qwen's LICENSE and a statement of modification (Apache-2.0 §4), and\\n       `base_model_relation: finetune`\\n     - my teacher, Qwen3.8-27B\\n     - credit to mlc-ai for the libraries\\n     - CC-BY-4.0 attribution for *Rights Nobody Has to Earn* by dhilipsiva\\n     - \\\"plus a private manuscript by dhilipsiva, not published\\\"\\n     - aggregate eval numbers\\n   - **Never** the dataset, caches or manuscript text.\\n3. Pin `LUCY_REV`, then run `zola build` with your site's zola 0.22.1.\\n4. Commit the site on `source`. **Pushing deploys it**, so I check with you first.\\n5. Commit nibli on `main`: the dataset code, tests, `lucy.md`, and my memory records.\\n   I push when you ask.\\n\\n## How I'll know it works\\n\\n- **nibli:** `just test-lucy`, `just clippy-lucy`, `just verify-lucy-plugin` (USAGE\\n  changed), `just check-lucy-memory`, then the full `just ci` in the background.\\n- **Runtimes:** the Step 0.5 numbers, recorded.\\n- **Dataset:**\\n  - manifest counts and gate drops\\n  - 30 sampled rows (I show you book rows only if you ask)\\n  - a canary grep and an independent 8-word rescan of the final `train.jsonl`\\n  - `git status` in the site, nibli and book repos shows nothing derived as tracked\\n- **Training:** the gate table for both files, and my smoke probes.\\n- **Browser, CPU path:** `zola serve`, then Playwright headless Chromium (no WebGPU,\\n  which forces the fallback).\\n  - I answer several questions in a row and stop cleanly; tokens/s and memory are\\n    recorded.\\n  - Switching personas clears history.\\n  - Your twins still load and answer.\\n- **Browser, WebGPU path:** Chrome on Windows at `http://localhost:1111/chat/`. Same\\n  questions; tokens/s for q4f16_1, and q4f32_1 forced once.\\n- **Afterwards** I write a note in my memory: sizes, gate numbers, speeds, and the HF\\n  revision.\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T08:31:45Z\",\"host\":\"DESKTOP-86I05G4\",\"source\":\"claude-code\",\"session\":\"0e43ab52-c3ec-4703-90f8-4af54eb3d290\",\"channel\":\"plan\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"slm\",\"wasm\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
